==English==
[[File:Rowan tree 20081002b.jpg|right|thumb|A European rowan]]

===Etymology 1===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*h₁rewdʰ-}}
{{der|en|sco|-}} and Northern English, possibly of {{der|en|gmq|-}} origin.  Possibly related to {{der|en|non|reynir}}, ({{cog|nb|rogn}}, {{cog|da|røn}}). Ultimately related to the root of {{m|en|red}}.

====Alternative forms====
* {{alter|en|roan||archaic}}

====Pronunciation====
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|en|/ˈɹəʊ.ən/}}
* {{a|Northern England|Scotland}} {{IPA|en|/ˈɹaʊ.ən/}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|en|/ˈɹaʊ.ən/|/ˈɹoʊ.ən/}}
* {{rhymes|en|əʊən|aʊən|s1=2}}

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# ''[[Sorbus aucuparia]]'', the [[European rowan]].
#: {{synonyms|en|mountain ash|wicken|wicky}}
# Any of various small [[deciduous]] [[tree]]s or [[shrub]]s of genus ''[[Sorbus]]'', belonging to the rose family, with [[pinnate]] leaves, [[corymb]]s of white flowers, and usually with orange-red berries.

